  "body": "Part of #308. Builds on #196 (work offset per setup) and the 3-2-1 alignment (#187).\n\n## Need\nCarrying stock from one setup into the next needs the rigid transform between the setups' part placements. `SetupDef { stock, wcs, datum_from }` (`crates/app/src/commands/setup.rs`) has none: M3.2 A deferred it (\"the transform is M3.3 ... rotation/flip matrices deliberately do not exist yet\") and M3.3 shipped posts instead.\n\n## Proposal\n- Store on each setup a rigid transform part -> setup frame (rotation + translation, finite-checked), defined from: the setup's work offset placement and orientation (#196, #187); presets for the common re-clamps (flip about X, flip about Y, rotate 90/180/270 about Z); or a datum transfer from another setup (`datum_from`).\n- An undoable `SetSetupTransform` command, saved and loaded; rigid only, rotation orthonormal by construction; a non-rigid or non-finite transform is refused by name at command creation.\n\n## Done means\nEach setup's transform round-trips through save/load and undo/redo; presets give the expected matrices (pinned); a document with no transform behaves exactly as today (implicit-setup law).\n",
